{
  "source": "Prompts/embrace-the-future-opener-v6.mp4",
  "duration": 197.312,
  "segments": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.32,
      "text": "It's going to cure diseases."
    },
    {
      "start": 2.08,
      "end": 3.24,
      "text": "It's going to take your job."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.84,
      "end": 5.36,
      "text": "It'll do the boring parts for you."
    },
    {
      "start": 5.84,
      "end": 6.74,
      "text": "It will hurt society."
    },
    {
      "start": 7.52,
      "end": 7.9,
      "text": "Who's right?"
    },
    {
      "start": 8.48,
      "end": 9.44,
      "text": "Nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 10.22,
      "end": 14.3,
      "text": "Up to this point, you've learned exactly how to use AI in your daily life."
    },
    {
      "start": 14.7,
      "end": 17.28,
      "text": "You understand the underlying engine running it,"
    },
    {
      "start": 17.48,
      "end": 19.48,
      "text": "which means that when the model behaves strangely,"
    },
    {
      "start": 20.2,
      "end": 22.98,
      "text": "that strange behavior actually makes perfect sense to you."
    },
    {
      "start": 23.34,
      "end": 26.6,
      "text": "Your initial goal for this course was to be smarter than the tool."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.08,
      "end": 28.14,
      "text": "Consider that done."
    },
    {
      "start": 28.74,
      "end": 31.08,
      "text": "But understanding how a tool works mechanically"
    },
    {
      "start": 31.08,
      "end": 35.02,
      "text": "doesn't automatically tell us how it will impact society in the long run."
    },
    {
      "start": 35.68,
      "end": 38.74,
      "text": "There's the optimist, who thinks AI is completely fantastic."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.68,
      "end": 42.08,
      "text": "There's the warrior, who was convinced it will hurt society."
    },
    {
      "start": 43.06,
      "end": 45.3,
      "text": "Here's the honest part, nobody knows."
    },
    {
      "start": 46.16,
      "end": 49.68,
      "text": "Not them, not us, not the people building AI."
    },
    {
      "start": 50.46,
      "end": 54.32,
      "text": "Centuries ago, map makers had to chart vast expanses of ocean"
    },
    {
      "start": 54.32,
      "end": 56.38,
      "text": "they simply did not understand yet."
    },
    {
      "start": 57.0,
      "end": 58.98,
      "text": "Whenever they reach the edges of their knowledge,"
    },
    {
      "start": 59.46,
      "end": 63.86,
      "text": "they would fill the blank waters with imaginary sea monsters and strange serpents."
    },
    {
      "start": 64.54,
      "end": 68.32,
      "text": "The future of AI is like the unknown parts of the ocean on those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 69.12,
      "end": 71.68,
      "text": "Warriors fill the unknown parts with AI monsters"
    },
    {
      "start": 71.68,
      "end": 75.24,
      "text": "that destroy jobs, hack systems, and take over the world."
    },
    {
      "start": 76.04,
      "end": 78.34,
      "text": "AI optimists look at the same unknown parts"
    },
    {
      "start": 78.34,
      "end": 81.32,
      "text": "and see easy, clear sailing through open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 81.92,
      "end": 84.34,
      "text": "Both the utopian and dystopian extremes"
    },
    {
      "start": 84.34,
      "end": 86.52,
      "text": "are just modern versions of those old maps."
    },
    {
      "start": 87.42,
      "end": 89.38,
      "text": "When people lack facts about a blank space,"
    },
    {
      "start": 89.86,
      "end": 92.2,
      "text": "they draw their own fears and hopes to fill it."
    },
    {
      "start": 92.9,
      "end": 96.96,
      "text": "History shows us that early sailors never actually encountered literal sea monsters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 97.56,
      "end": 100.04,
      "text": "but they also rarely got easy, clear sailing."
    },
    {
      "start": 100.8,
      "end": 103.54,
      "text": "Instead, they usually found something entirely unexpected."
    },
    {
      "start": 104.46,
      "end": 105.88,
      "text": "Consider Ferdinand Magellan."
    },
    {
      "start": 106.42,
      "end": 109.7,
      "text": "He never actually set off to sail around the world,"
    },
    {
      "start": 110.12,
      "end": 112.78,
      "text": "but his crew ended up achieving exactly that."
    },
    {
      "start": 112.78,
      "end": 115.82,
      "text": "And Magellan himself met a tragic end,"
    },
    {
      "start": 116.24,
      "end": 119.46,
      "text": "dying before the historic voyage was even completed."
    },
    {
      "start": 120.26,
      "end": 121.14,
      "text": "Did he expect either?"
    },
    {
      "start": 121.78,
      "end": 122.02,
      "text": "No."
    },
    {
      "start": 122.7,
      "end": 124.0,
      "text": "So as we move forward,"
    },
    {
      "start": 124.24,
      "end": 126.9,
      "text": "we are going to take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 127.84,
      "end": 128.74,
      "text": "We will look at the monsters,"
    },
    {
      "start": 129.5,
      "end": 131.06,
      "text": "and we will look at the open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 131.7,
      "end": 134.76,
      "text": "Right now, there is only one absolute certainty."
    },
    {
      "start": 135.32,
      "end": 136.92,
      "text": "AI is here to stay."
    },
    {
      "start": 137.56,
      "end": 139.88,
      "text": "That doesn't mean it will keep getting better forever,"
    },
    {
      "start": 140.36,
      "end": 141.94,
      "text": "just that it isn't going away."
    },
    {
      "start": 142.52,
      "end": 147.34,
      "text": "Because this technology is a permanent fixture with a trajectory we can't fully predict,"
    },
    {
      "start": 147.94,
      "end": 151.28,
      "text": "our best path forward is to prepare for unexpected realities"
    },
    {
      "start": 151.8,
      "end": 153.86,
      "text": "rather than clinging to extreme predictions."
    },
    {
      "start": 154.9,
      "end": 157.54,
      "text": "This roadmap shows what we'll explore in this section,"
    },
    {
      "start": 157.92,
      "end": 159.0,
      "text": "embrace the future."
    },
    {
      "start": 159.88,
      "end": 160.92,
      "text": "One, the argument."
    },
    {
      "start": 161.72,
      "end": 163.62,
      "text": "The loudest voices, why they disagree,"
    },
    {
      "start": 164.24,
      "end": 166.42,
      "text": "and why the speed makes the argument louder."
    },
    {
      "start": 167.52,
      "end": 169.66,
      "text": "Two, monsters and open water."
    },
    {
      "start": 169.66,
      "end": 175.06,
      "text": "The honest case for worry alongside the real world upside that has already happened."
    },
    {
      "start": 175.88,
      "end": 177.74,
      "text": "Three, where it lands on you,"
    },
    {
      "start": 178.18,
      "end": 180.84,
      "text": "how AI acts, how work may change,"
    },
    {
      "start": 181.52,
      "end": 182.66,
      "text": "the bill for all that math,"
    },
    {
      "start": 183.18,
      "end": 184.98,
      "text": "and what history teaches about predictions."
    },
    {
      "start": 186.38,
      "end": 187.94,
      "text": "Take both views of the map seriously."
    },
    {
      "start": 188.92,
      "end": 190.4,
      "text": "Nobody has a map of what's coming."
    },
    {
      "start": 191.0,
      "end": 192.8,
      "text": "You're ready to sail into the blank space."
    }
  ],
